WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.897
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:08.793
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:18.943
Unit twelve: B2 First: Word Formation and Key Word Transformations. Today you will change word forms and rewrite sentences with a given word.

4
00:00:19.243 --> 00:00:21.989
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:26.178
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:28.250
Word formation.

7
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:33.154
Word formation means changing a word with a prefix or suffix.

8
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.645
Part 3 is word formation.

9
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.879
Your turn. Say: Word formation.

10
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:42.874
Word formation.

11
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:44.595
Prefix.

12
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:47.862
Prefix means letters before a word.

13
00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.974
Un- is a prefix.

14
00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.050
Your turn. Say: Prefix.

15
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.982
Prefix.

16
00:00:57.717 --> 00:00:58.787
Suffix.

17
00:00:59.783 --> 00:01:01.818
Suffix means letters after a word.

18
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:03.975
-ness is a suffix.

19
00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:07.189
Your turn. Say: Suffix.

20
00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:11.197
Suffix.

21
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:12.847
Negative.

22
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.140
Negative means expressing 'no' or 'not'.

23
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.204
Make the word negative.

24
00:01:18.817 --> 00:01:21.121
Your turn. Say: Negative.

25
00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:24.852
Negative.

26
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:26.850
Transformation.

27
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:31.161
Transformation means a rewritten sentence with the same meaning.

28
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.541
Complete the transformation.

29
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.988
Your turn. Say: Transformation.

30
00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.171
Transformation.

31
00:01:41.917 --> 00:01:42.813
Key word.

32
00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:46.931
Key word means a word you must use without changing it.

33
00:01:47.517 --> 00:01:48.854
Use the key word.

34
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.835
Your turn. Say: Key word.

35
00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.480
Key word.

36
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:57.345
Similar meaning.

37
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.255
Similar meaning means nearly the same meaning.

38
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.211
Keep the similar meaning.

39
00:02:03.817 --> 00:02:06.283
Your turn. Say: Similar meaning.

40
00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:10.367
Similar meaning.

41
00:02:11.117 --> 00:02:12.211
Word limit.

42
00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:15.913
Word limit means the allowed number of words.

43
00:02:16.517 --> 00:02:18.238
Use two to five words.

44
00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.270
Your turn. Say: Word limit.

45
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.216
Word limit.

46
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.581
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.417 --> 00:02:33.008
Visal, how does word formation work?

48
00:02:34.117 --> 00:02:45.813
You see a word in capitals at the end of a line and change it to fit the gap. Decide the part of speech, then add a suffix or prefix, and check whether it must be negative or plural.

49
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:49.311
What about key word transformations?

50
00:02:50.417 --> 00:02:58.700
You rewrite a sentence so it means the same, using a given key word and two to five words. You must not change the key word.

51
00:02:59.783 --> 00:03:01.551
What are common structures?

52
00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:18.224
They test passive, conditionals, reported speech, comparison, modals and phrasal verbs. For example, I haven't seen her since 2020 becomes the last time I saw her was in 2020.

53
00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:20.809
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:26.192
Grammar focus: Strategy: part of speech, then structure.

55
00:03:26.492 --> 00:03:27.737
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.519
The weather was unpredictable (PREDICT).

57
00:03:31.417 --> 00:03:34.313
'I'll help you,' he said. He offered to help me.

58
00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:43.724
In Part 3 decide the part of speech and check for negative or plural forms. In Part 4 keep the key word and use a structure that gives the same meaning.

59
00:03:44.483 --> 00:03:47.960
Be careful! Don't say: I change the key word.

60
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.853
Say: I keep the key word.

61
00:03:52.153 --> 00:03:54.013
Never change the key word.

62
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.580
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:58.367 --> 00:03:59.844
Changing Words.

64
00:04:00.144 --> 00:04:02.701
Bora sees the word PREDICT at the end of a line.

65
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.487
The gap needs an adjective that means 'cannot be known beforehand'.

66
00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.161
She adds the prefix un- and the suffix -able.

67
00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:15.292
In the transformation she must use the key word OFFERED.

68
00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.497
She writes a sentence that means the same.

69
00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.741
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:24.583 --> 00:04:26.792
In word formation you change the blank.

71
00:04:27.092 --> 00:04:31.256
A, form of the word. B, topic. C, spelling of names only.

72
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.765
The answer is A: form of the word.

73
00:04:37.917 --> 00:04:39.545
A key word must be blank.

74
00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:44.113
A, translated. B, used without changing. C, deleted.

75
00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:50.572
The answer is B: used without changing.

76
00:04:51.717 --> 00:04:54.076
Unpredictable has the prefix blank.

77
00:04:54.376 --> 00:04:57.136
A, re-. B, pre-. C, un-.

78
00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.224
The answer is C: un-.

79
00:05:03.383 --> 00:05:05.731
A transformation must keep the blank.

80
00:05:06.031 --> 00:05:10.323
A, same meaning. B, same length only. C, same colour.

81
00:05:13.867 --> 00:05:15.971
The answer is A: same meaning.

82
00:05:17.117 --> 00:05:19.673
Words allowed in a transformation: blank.

83
00:05:19.973 --> 00:05:23.476
A, ten. B, two to five. C, one.

84
00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.358
The answer is B: two to five.

85
00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:34.020
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:34.883 --> 00:05:37.220
How do you answer a key word transformation?

87
00:05:46.017 --> 00:05:47.447
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:47.747 --> 00:06:00.770
I read the first sentence and the key word. I decide which structure gives the same meaning, such as the passive or reported speech. I write two to five words, including the key word, and check the grammar.

89
00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.721
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:03.617 --> 00:06:08.997
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: part of speech, then structure.

91
00:06:09.297 --> 00:06:14.399
Today's value is logical rigor. Follow your reasoning wherever it honestly leads.

92
00:06:14.699 --> 00:06:17.526
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:17.826 --> 00:06:20.583
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

